{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbEpYnXSY4qcUPM8ui6A", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Avp9XKjAHDyV3fmwho1M8s", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/tmp/mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx/claude-config/projects/-tmp-mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx-ledgerline/memory/payments-live-env-var.md", "content": "---\nname: payments-live-env-var\ndescription: Hazard \u2014 app silently uses a fake payment gateway unless PAYMENTS_LIVE=1 is set\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nThe app silently falls back to a fake/sandbox payment gateway unless the env var `PAYMENTS_LIVE=1` is set. There's no warning or log line when this happens. As of 2026-10-01, the `PAYMENTS_LIVE` check isn't anywhere in the ledgerline repo source (it may live in a dependency, a config layer, or the deploy environment). The only related reference is `SANDBOX = \"https://sandbox.payments.example/v1/charges\"` in `tests/test_payments.py`.\n\n**Why:** The user lost two hours debugging payments that were silently hitting the fake gateway.\n\n**How to apply:** When payments act strangely (charges don't show up, responses look canned), check `PAYMENTS_LIVE` first. Mention it whenever running or debugging payment flows.\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 202, "cache_read_input_tokens": 18988, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 202}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5d7651a8-edf7-44db-8808-57205bd516ac", "uuid": "01cff8ba-7165-498d-b4cc-f1879678a8f8", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T08:56:55.622Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbEpYSgxtJGdE37Nsw83", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01Avp9XKjAHDyV3fmwho1M8s": {"file_path": "/tmp/mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx/claude-config/projects/-tmp-mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx-ledgerline/memory/payments-live-env-var.md", "content": "---\nname: payments-live-env-var\ndescription: Hazard \u2014 app silently uses a fake payment gateway unless PAYMENTS_LIVE=1 is set\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nThe app silently falls back to a fake/sandbox payment gateway unless the env var `PAYMENTS_LIVE=1` is set. There's no warning or log line when this happens. As of 2026-10-01, the `PAYMENTS_LIVE` check isn't anywhere in the ledgerline repo source (it may live in a dependency, a config layer, or the deploy environment). The only related reference is `SANDBOX = \"https://sandbox.payments.example/v1/charges\"` in `tests/test_payments.py`.\n\n**Why:** The user lost two hours debugging payments that were silently hitting the fake gateway.\n\n**How to apply:** When payments act strangely (charges don't show up, responses look canned), check `PAYMENTS_LIVE` first. Mention it whenever running or debugging payment flows.\n"}}}
