{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Avp9XKjAHDyV3fmwho1M8s", "type": "tool_result", "content": "File created successfully at: /tmp/mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx/claude-config/projects/-tmp-mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx-ledgerline/memory/payments-live-env-var.md"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5d7651a8-edf7-44db-8808-57205bd516ac", "uuid": "fce4504e-aa24-4471-9a42-deaa3e108024", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T08:56:55.754Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "create", "filePath": "/tmp/mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx/claude-config/projects/-tmp-mte-nk-env-var-dpp4ovqx-ledgerline/memory/payments-live-env-var.md", "content": "---\nname: payments-live-env-var\ndescription: Hazard \u2014 app silently uses a fake payment gateway unless PAYMENTS_LIVE=1 is set\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 5d7651a8-edf7-44db-8808-57205bd516ac\n  modified: 2026-10-01T08:56:55.692Z\n---\n\nThe app silently falls back to a fake/sandbox payment gateway unless the env var `PAYMENTS_LIVE=1` is set. There's no warning or log line when this happens. As of 2026-10-01, the `PAYMENTS_LIVE` check isn't anywhere in the ledgerline repo source (it may live in a dependency, a config layer, or the deploy environment). The only related reference is `SANDBOX = \"https://sandbox.payments.example/v1/charges\"` in `tests/test_payments.py`.\n\n**Why:** The user lost two hours debugging payments that were silently hitting the fake gateway.\n\n**How to apply:** When payments act strangely (charges don't show up, responses look canned), check `PAYMENTS_LIVE` first. Mention it whenever running or debugging payment flows.\n", "structuredPatch": [], "originalFile": null, "userModified": false, "memdirStamped": true}}
